{
  "mn44:0.1": "Middle Discourses 44 ",
  "mn44:0.2": "The Shorter Elaboration ",
  "mn44:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn44:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn44:1.3": "Then the layman Visākha went to see the nun Dhammadinnā, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to her: ",
  "mn44:2.1": "“Ma’am, they speak of this thing called ‘substantial reality’. ",
  "mn44:2.2": "What is this substantial reality that the Buddha spoke of?” ",
  "mn44:2.3": "“Visākha, the Buddha said that these five grasping aggregates are substantial reality. ",
  "mn44:2.4": "That is, the grasping aggregates of form, feeling, perception, choices, and consciousness. ",
  "mn44:2.5": "The Buddha said that these five grasping aggregates are substantial reality.” ",
  "mn44:2.6": "Saying “Good, ma’am,” Visākha approved and agreed with what Dhammadinnā said. Then he asked another question: ",
  "mn44:3.1": "“Ma’am, they speak of this thing called ‘the origin of substantial reality’. ",
  "mn44:3.2": "What is the origin of substantial reality that the Buddha spoke of?” ",
  "mn44:3.3": "“It’s the craving that leads to future lives, mixed up with relishing and greed, taking pleasure there wherever it alights. That is, ",
  "mn44:3.4": "craving for sensual pleasures, craving for continued existence, and craving for nonexistence. ",
  "mn44:3.5": "The Buddha said that this is the origin of substantial reality.” ",
  "mn44:4